[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-integration-bug-trial-3[0m[0m
Fixed — real validator returns **EXCELLENT (1.0)**, all 6 trials pass.

**Root cause** (`checkout.py:13–26`): the flow was *check stock → charge → decrement*. All 12 concurrent orders passed `check_stock` against the same 5 items, charged, then only 5 decrements could succeed — the rest were charged with no item delivered (ghost charges) and `charged != successful × price` broke.

**Changes:**

- `checkout.py` — reordered to **reserve → charge → release-on-failure**: reserve stock atomically first; charge only after the item is secured; release the reservation back to stock if payment fails.
- `inventory.py` — added `asyncio.Lock` and two new methods (`reserve`, `release`); the lock serializes all stock mutations so stock can never go negative. Existing public interface (`check_stock`, `decrement`, `increment`, `stock`) kept intact; `decrement`/`increment` also lock-guarded now.

**Invariants now hold:** `stock == 5 − successful` (never negative), `charged == successful × 100.0`, zero duplicate charges across all 6 seeded trials. `payments.py` untouched; `main.py` unchanged and prints no ERROR lines.
